speechtext:
1.	Mr. L. A. Bouliane, N.P., of La Malbaie, Que., was appointed for the county of Charlevoix and Mr. Alfred Larouche (Wenceslas) of Grandes Bergeronnes, Que., for the county of Saguenay.
2.	Appointed by the Honourable the Minister of Trade and Commerce.
3.	Mr. Bouliane, commissioner for Charlevoix, is a notary, 68 years of age, and resides at La Malbaie, Que. Mr. Larouche (Wenceslas) commissioner for Saguenay, is a contractor, about 33 years of age, and resides at Grandes Bergeronnes, Que.
4.	Each commissioner allowed an allowance of $600 to cover organization expenses and for viseing of the returns made by the enumerators; checking them and forwarding to Ottawa; verification of enumerators' accounts and the general supervision of the census within the district over which they are appointed as commissioner the following rates are provided:
One cent for each name on the "population" schedule;
Three cents for each "agricultural" schedule;
One cent for each entry on the "animal and animal products, not on farm" schedule;
One cent for each record of blind and deaf persons;
One cent for each record of merchandising and service establishment.
5.	Enumerators have not yet been appointed.

